    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0182",
      "sequence": 194,
      "meaning": "Rāvaṇa summons Meghanāda, instructing him so as to inflame both strength and enmity: the gods who pride themselves on courage in battle must be defeated, bound and brought before him. After issuing orders to all, Rāvaṇa himself sets out with mace in hand; the earth reels, pregnant celestial women miscarry at his roar, and the enraged gods hide in Mount Meru’s caves. He finds the guardians’ beautiful realms deserted, bellows repeatedly, abuses and challenges the gods, and roams the universe intoxicated with martial pride without finding a rival. Sun, moon, wind, Varuṇa, Kubera, fire, Time, Yama, Kinnaras, Siddhas, humans, gods and Nāgas—all embodied creation—come under his control and humbly obey. Rāvaṇa rules as emperor through his own counsel and seizes many beautiful celestial, Yakṣa, Gandharva, human, Kinnara and Nāga maidens by force.",
