    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0183",
      "sequence": 195,
      "meaning": "Whatever Rāvaṇa tells Indrajit has seemingly already been accomplished. Śiva now describes the deeds of those who received the earlier commands. Terrifying bands of sinful demons torment the gods, take many shapes through illusion and cause every disturbance that can uproot dharma or oppose the Vedas. Wherever they find cows or Brahmins, they burn towns, villages and cities. Good conduct disappears; no one honours gods, Brahmins or teachers, and nowhere even in dreams can one hear of devotion to Hari, sacrifice, austerity, knowledge, Vedas or Purāṇas.",
