    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0184",
      "sequence": 196,
      "meaning": "Villains multiply—thieves, gamblers, libertines who covet others’ wealth and wives. They honour neither mother, father nor gods and instead force holy people to serve them; Śiva says that all creatures of such conduct should be known as demons. Seeing the extreme decline of dharma, Earth becomes deeply frightened and distressed. Mountains, rivers and oceans do not weigh on her as heavily as a single person who harms others. Terrified of Rāvaṇa, she cannot express how every dharma has been inverted. Taking a cow’s form, she goes weeping to the hosts of gods and sages, but none can accomplish anything for her grief.",
