    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0185",
      "sequence": 197,
      "meaning": "The assembled gods deliberate where to find the Lord and cry for help: some point to Vaikuṇṭha, others say he dwells in the Milk Ocean. Śiva answers that the Lord appears wherever devotion and love fill a heart: Hari pervades everything equally and manifests through love. What place, time, direction or quarter could lack him? He fills moving and unmoving creation yet is detached from all, appearing through love as fire appears. All accept Śiva’s words and praise them; Brahmā rejoices, his body thrills and tears flow. Joining his hands, the steadfast one begins an attentive hymn.",
